 "caption": "Blockbuster laughed at a $50 million offer.\n\nIn 2000, according to Fortune, the Netflix founders tried to sell their startup to Blockbuster for $50 million and were laughed out of the room. Blockbuster had more than 9,000 stores by 2004 and made $800 million (16% of revenue) from late fees alone in 2000. It filed for bankruptcy in 2010, and Fortune says it is now down to a single store.\n\nBlockbuster wasn't careless. It was making money the old way, so the new way looked like a toy. Your customers are already ordering on their phones. If they can't do it with you, they go to someone who lets them.\n\nCould a customer order from you tonight without calling? DM us the word ORDER and we'll check your site on a phone for you.\n\n#moodbod #websitedesign #smallbusinessnamibia #windhoek #namibia\n\nSources: Fortune, \"Netflix cofounder Marc Randolph recalls Blockbuster rejecting chance to buy it\" (14 Apr 2023); Mental Floss, \"15 Fast-Forward Facts About Blockbuster Video\".",
